K	97	tRP (row precharge)	Cycles needed to close an open row before a different row in the same bank can be opened.	~Auto	~Auto (XMP value)	~Lower after XMP is stable, then test	~Lower after XMP is stable, then test	~Lower after XMP is stable, then test	Change one timing at a time and test with a memory stress test (TestMem5 with an extreme/absolut config, Karhu, or y-cruncher) for at least an hour before trusting it. Memory errors corrupt files silently.	One of the timings that most affects memory latency, which shows up directly in CPU-bound 1% lows. Tightening it from the XMP value can give a few percent in CPU-bound games.	Smaller effect unless the game is CPU-bound.	Small for most apps. Memory-heavy work (compression, simulation) benefits.	XMP timings are loose on purpose so every kit boots. Most kits have headroom, but each kit is different.	reasoning	From how the hardware works; not measured. Workload-dependent effects: test them.	
